# Cargo build artifacts.
/target

# `Cargo.lock` is intentionally COMMITTED.
#
# This workspace produces binaries (a client, and a server crate later), so the
# lockfile pins the exact resolution of GPUI's very large transitive tree. A
# git dependency already pins GPUI itself via `rev`, but its ~700 transitive
# crates would otherwise float on every build, and upstream Zed bumps them
# daily. Committing `Cargo.lock` is the standard Cargo guidance for
# applications and is what makes a clean checkout reproducible -- which is
# precisely what PLAN.md section 8 Phase 0 asks for ("a window opens on Windows
# from a clean checkout").
#
# A future `sh_nexus_wire`/`sh_nexus_server` library split would move the
# question to per-crate lockfiles; not a Phase 0 concern.

